which is true since  $4b^2k>4k$ . Since  $4D$  is a square, by the above we must have  $4D = (2b^2k-b)^2$ , which becomes  $b^2=4k$  after simplification. Therefore,  $b=2x$  for some  $x \in \mathbb{N}$ , so  $k=x^2$ , so  $a=x, 8x^4-x$ . Therefore,  $(a,b)=(x,2x),(8x^4-x,2x)$  for any  $x\in \mathbb{N}$ . 

