Vieta jumping from the initial equation involving  $k$  does not work since the equation is not symmetric in  $a$  and  $b$ ; in order to Vieta jump we need to be able to jump in both elements of the pair to keep decreasing. The intuition then is to see what  $b$  can be. It is easy to see from size that  $b$  must be rather small compared to  $a$ , so for example if  $b=2$  we want to find when  $\frac{a^2}{8a-7}$  is a positive integer. From here, the obvious approach is to use the quadratic formula and discriminant.</details>

