Observe that if  $P(x)$  and  $Q(x)$  are solutions, then  $aP(x) +bP(x)$  are solutions for any  $a, b \in \mathbb R$ . Furthermore, it is easy to see that  $P$  must be even.

Letting  $a=-2x, b = 3x, c = 6x$ , we must have   $$ \sum_{n \geq 0} a_n((-5x)^n + (-3x)^n + (8x)^n)= \sum_{n \geq 0} a_n(2 \cdot (7x)^n). $$   Observe that  $8^7-3^7-5^7 > 2 \cdot 7^7$ , so by comparing the leading coefficients, we must have  $\deg P = 2$  or  $\deg P = 4$ . Thus,  $P(x) = mx^4+nx^2$  for any  $m, n \in \mathbb R$  are the solutions, which indeed work.

