Assume that  $x > 2$  and note then that either  $y - 1$  or  $y + 1$  is equal to  $2^{x-1}m$  for some  $m$  coprime to 2. Let  $y - 1 = 2^{x-1}m \iff y = 2^{x-1}m + 1$ . Then we have,
