Note by weighted AM-GM that  $a^ab^bc^cd^d \leq a \cdot a + b \cdot b + c \cdot c + d \cdot d$ . It is hence enough to prove that
\begin{align*}
	(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2)(a + 2b + 3c + 4d) &< 1 
	\iff (a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2)(a + 2b + 3c + 4d) &< (a + b + c + d)^3.
\end{align*}
Expanding, this is equivalent to 
\begin{align*}
        (a^3 + 2b^3 + 3c^3 + 4d^3) + (ab^2 + ac^2 + ad^2) + 2(ba^2 + bc^2 + bd^2) + 3(ca^2 + cb^2 + cd^2) 
        + 4(da^2 + db^2 + dc^2) < (a^3 + b^3 + c^3 + d^3) + 3(ab^2 + ac^2 + ad^2) + 3(ba^2 + bc^2 + bd^2) 
         + 3(ca^2 + cb^2 + cd^2) + 3(da^2 + db^2 + dc^2) + 6(abc + abd + acd + bcd),
\end{align*}
or
\begin{align*}
	(b^3 + 2c^3 + 3d^3) + (da^2 + db^2 + dc^2) &< 2(ab^2 + ac^2 + ad^2) + (ba^2 + bc^2 + bd^2) + 6(abc + abd + acd + bcd).
\end{align*}
This last inequality is insanely weak: we have
\begin{align*}
	b^3 &\leq ab^2 
	2c^3 &\leq 2c^2a 
	3d^3 &\leq 3abc 
	da^2 &\leq ba^2 
	db^2 &\leq abc 
	dc^2 &\leq abc 
	0 &< abc.
\end{align*}
Summing them gives 
\begin{align*}
	(b^3 + 2c^3 + 3d^3) + (da^2 + db^2 + dc^2) &< ab^2 + 2c^2 + ba^2 + 5abc,
\end{align*}
which trivially implies the desired.  $\Box$

