This problem is fairly similar to a problem I set in a Codeforces contest two weeks ago [here]("https://codeforces.com/contest/1404/problem/D"). I hear some contestants were able to draw inspiration from it to solve this P3, so you're welcome :P

Let's consider all the pairs of pebbles that have a total weight of  $4n + 1$ . There are exactly  $2n$  such pairs. Consider a graph on  $n$  vertices and add an edge between vertices  $x$  and  $y$  if some pair contains pebbles of those colors. We allow loops and multiple edges. Consider a connected component of the graph with  $k$  vertices, then all vertices have degree  $4$ , so the component has  $2k$  edges and admits a eulerian circuit.

