now we simply finish the problem:
the circle centered at  $T$  and radius  $TD$  is called  $\omega$ . we have to prove  $\odot ADC$ , $\odot EXD$  and  $\omega$  are coaxial.  $S$  is the miquel point of  $BCEF$ . the inverse of line  $AC$  with respect to  $\omega$  is  $\odot BSD$ . let  $BS \cap AC = N$ . 
\[\angle ABX=\angle B-\angle C=\angle ETC \implies \text{BX is tangent to circle BFT}\]
since \[\angle SEX=\angle STB=\angle SBX \implies \text{SEXB is cyclic}\]

now by power of point we have:
\[NE \times NX=NS \times NB=NA \times NC\]
so we get that  $N$  and  $D$  have the same power of point wrt the three circles  $\odot ADC$ ,  $\odot EXD$  and  $\omega$ .  $\blacksquare$  

