\begin{align*}
\frac{f(a)}{a}+\frac{f(b)}{b}&\leq\frac{2}{ab}
\frac{f(c)}{c}+\frac{f(d)}{d}&\leq\frac{2}{cd}
\frac{f(a)}{a}+\frac{f(d)}{d}&>\frac{2}{ad}
\frac{f(b)}{b}+\frac{f(c)}{c}&>\frac{2}{ab}.
\end{align*}
Adding the first two inequalities and subtracting the last two gives  $2\left(\frac{1}{a}-\frac{1}{c}\right)\left(\frac{1}{b}-\frac{1}{d}\right)>0$ . Thus  $(a-c)(b-d)>0$  and similarly,  $(a-d)(b-c)>0$ . WLOG  $a<b$ . Taking  $a<c<b$  gives  $d>b$  and  $d<a$ , a contradiction. Thus  $g(x)=x$  for all  $x$ .

