<details><summary>Click to expand</summary>**Lemma.**
    Let  $\omega$  be a circle with diameter  $BF$ , and let  $A$  and  $D$  be points on  $\omega$ . Let  $C$  be on  $BF$  such that with  $S = BD \cap AC$ ,  $BC=CS$ . Let  $E$  be the second intersection of  $AC$  with  $\omega$ . Let  $G$  be the antipode of  $D$ . Let  $P$  be on  $AE$  such that directed angles  $\angle PDB = \angle EBF$ . Let  $X$  be the point on  $BD$  such that  $XA \perp AE$ . Then  $(BPX)$  is tangent to  $PD$ .
