I claim that  $a_n\ge\left\lfloor \dfrac{3n}{2} \right\rfloor$  for all  $n$ . Note that our problem condition is equivalent to the case when  $n=2023$ .

Firstly note that  $(x_i+x_j)\left(\dfrac{1}{x_i}+\dfrac{1}{x_j}\right)=1+1+\dfrac{x_i}{x_j}+\dfrac{x_j}{x_i}>1+1+(2)=4$  where the last inequality follows from AM-GM (note that the equality case cannot occur as it forces  $x_i=x_j$ ).

Now, we have our following base cases.  $a_1=1\ge \left\lfloor \dfrac{3\cdot 1}{2} \right\rfloor$ , and  $a_2=\sqrt{(x_1+x_2)\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\dfrac{1}{x_2}\right)}>\sqrt{4}=2\implies a_2\ge 3=\left\lfloor \dfrac{3\cdot 2}{2} \right\rfloor$ .

Now we proceed using strong induction. We divide the problem into the cases based on the parity of  $n$ . $\bullet\; \textbf{Case 1:}$   $n$  is odd,  $n=2m+1$ . Note that using strong induction, we have that  $(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)\ge (3m)^2$ .

\begin{align*}
    a_{2m+1}&=\sqrt{(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m+1})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}\right)}
    &=\sqrt{(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)+(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}\right)+(x_{2m+1})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)+1}
    &\ge\sqrt{(3m)^2+2\sqrt{(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}\right)\cdot(x_{2m+1})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)}+1}
    &=\sqrt{(3m)^2+2(3m)+1}
    &=3m+1
    &=\left\lfloor \dfrac{3\cdot(2m+1)}{2} \right\rfloor
. \square\end{align*} $\bullet\; \textbf{Case 2:}$   $n$  is even,  $n=2m+2$ . We use  $(x_{2m+1}+x_{2m+2})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+2}}\right)>4$  as we proved earlier.

\begin{align*}
    a_{2m+2}&=\sqrt{(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m+2})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+2}}\right)}
    &=\sqrt{(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)+(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+2}}\right)+(x_{2m+1}+x_{2m+2})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)+(x_{2m+1}+x_{2m+2})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+2}}\right)}
    &\ge\sqrt{(3m)^2+2\sqrt{(x_1+\cdots+x_{2m})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+2}}\right)\cdot(x_{2m+1}+x_{2m+2})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_1}+\cdots+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m}}\right)}+(x_{2m+1}+x_{2m+2})\left(\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+1}}+\dfrac{1}{x_{2m+2}}\right)}
    &>\sqrt{(3m)^2+2(3m)(2)+4}
    &=3m+2
.\end{align*}

This gives us that  $a_{2m+2}>3m+2$  and as  $a_{2m+2}$  is given to be an integer, we get that  $a_{2m+2}\ge 3m+3=\left\lfloor \dfrac{3\cdot(2m+2)}{2} \right\rfloor$ .  $\square$ Thus assembling the cases, we get that  $a_n\ge\left\lfloor \dfrac{3n}{2} \right\rfloor$  and our claim is proved and we are done. :stretcher: :D

