We claim that  $a_{n+2}>a_n+2.$ Proof: We can write  $a_{n+2}$  as 
\begin{align*}
&\sqrt{\sum^{n+2}_{i=1}x_i\sum^{n+2}_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}}
&=\sqrt{\left(\sum^{n}_{i=1}x_i+x_{n+1}+x_{n+2}\right)\left(\sum^{n}_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)}
&=\sqrt{\sum^n_{i=1}x_i\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i+(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)}
&=\sqrt{a_n^2+(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i+2+\frac{x_{n+1}}{x_{n+2}}+\frac{x_{n+2}}{x_{n+1}}}.
\end{align*}
Now since  $x_{n+1}$  and  $x_{n+2}$  are distinct positive reals we can apply AM-GM to get that   $$ \sqrt{a_n^2+(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i+2+\frac{x_{n+1}}{x_{n+2}}+\frac{x_{n+2}}{x_{n+1}}} $$    $$ >\sqrt{a_n^2+(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i+4}. $$   

Hence, it suffices to prove that 
\begin{align*}
&\sqrt{a_n^2+(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i+4}>a_n+2
&\Longleftrightarrow (x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i\geq 4a_n.
\end{align*}

Now note that since all of the  $x_i$ 's are positive reals we can apply AM-GM on the left-hand side to get
\begin{align*}
(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i&\geq 2\sqrt{\left(\sum^n_{i=1}x_i\right)\left(\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}\right)(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)}
&=2\sqrt{a_n^2(x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)}
&> 2\sqrt{4a_n^2}=4a_n.
\end{align*}

Hence, since we have shown that   $$ (x_{n+1}+x_{n+2})\sum^n_{i=1}\frac{1}{x_i}+\left(\frac{1}{x_{n+1}}+\frac{1}{x_{n+2}}\right)\sum^n_{i=1}x_i\geq 4a_n, $$   we have shown that  $a_{n+2}>a_n+2.$ Since all of the  $a_i$  terms are integers we know that  $a_{n+2}\geq a_n+3.$  Therefore,   $$ a_{2023}\geqslant a_{2021}+3\geq a_{2019}+6\geqslant\cdots\geqslant a_1+3\cdot 1011=3034, $$   so we are done.

