Solve the system of equations:
 $
\begin{matrix}
|x+y| + |1-x| = 6  |x+y+1| + |1-y| = 4.
\end{matrix}
$

candidates:
Solution:
\begin{align*}
y &= \frac{\tan(x-u)+\tan x +\tan(x+u)}{\tan(x-u)\tan x \tan(x+u)} =\dfrac{\dfrac{\tan x - \tan u}{1+\tan x \tan u} + \tan x + \dfrac{\tan x + \tan u}{1-\tan x \tan u}}{\dfrac{\tan x - \tan u}{1+\tan x \tan u} \cdot \tan x \cdot \dfrac{\tan x + \tan u}{1-\tan x \tan u}}
&= \frac{(\tan x - \tan u)(1 - \tan x \tan u) + \tan x (1 + \tan x \tan u)(1 - \tan x \tan u) + (\tan x + \tan u)(1 + \tan x \tan u)}{(\tan x - \tan u)\cdot \tan x \cdot (\tan x + \tan u)}
&= \frac{2\tan x + 2 \tan x\tan^2 u + \tan x(1- \tan^2x\tan^2u)}{\tan x (\tan^2x - \tan^2 u)}
&= \frac{2 + 2 \tan^2 u + 1- \tan^2x\tan^2u}{\tan^2x - \tan^2 u} = \frac{3 + 2 \tan^2 u - \tan^2x\tan^2u}{\tan^2x - \tan^2 u}
&= \frac{ \tan^2 x - \tan^2 u + 3 - \tan^2 x + 3 \tan^2 u - \tan^2x\tan^2u}{\tan^2x - \tan^2 u}
&= \frac{ (\tan^2 x - \tan^2 u) + (3 - \tan^2 x)(1 + \tan^2 u)}{\tan^2x - \tan^2 u}
&= 1 + \frac{ (3 - \tan^2 x)(1 + \tan^2 u)}{\tan^2x - \tan^2 u} = 1 + \frac{ (3 - \tan^2 x)(1 + \tan^2 u)}{(\tan^2x - 3) - ( \tan^2 u-3)}= 1 + \frac{ 1 + \tan^2 u}{-1 - \dfrac{\tan^2 u-3}{3 - \tan^2 x}}
\end{align*}
Because  $y$  does not depend on  $x$ , we have  $\tan^2 u - 3 = 0$ , which implies  $u = k\pi \pm \frac{\pi}{3}, k\in\mathbb{Z}$  and  $y = -3$ .

